WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:09.060
So, I just had a quick meeting in Ventura,
Oxnard, early in the morning.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:15.420
If you recognize this place -- that, right
there, is Raffi's place.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.580
One of the best restaurants in the world.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:27.710
Came from Ventura, visited my dad, went to
Delicate Cosmetics, our good family there.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.710
What a business!

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:38.969
Great success story on what they've built
as a family.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:46.989
They've built an incredible business for themselves,
making makeup for some of the big companies

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:47.989
in the world.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:51.780
And then Tom and I are out here getting in
the car to head back to the airport, after

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.780
having Raffi's place.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.390
We've got to drop off the rental car.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:01.920
You know, I was in Ventura this morning and
Oxnard, California and we were having a conversation

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.100
with some of these guys and one of the questions
that I was asked was, "Pat, tell me about

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.100
confidence.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.190
What can I do to improve my confidence?"

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:17.000
And I said, you know, everybody is asking
for like a seven-step process to having more

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.210
confidence, right?

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.220
But, to me, confidence stems from a couple
of different things.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.750
I'm going to talk about two different things
in this video, one of them being how to be

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.010
more confident.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:33.880
Listen, no matter you do, a person who's a
criminal who's extremely confident, a man

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:41.010
who's a player who's extremely confident with
women, a businessman who's extremely good

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:52.950
at what he does with business, a person who
runs anything -- a coach, an athlete -- anybody

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.050
who's extremely confident at what they do,
it's not just a natural state.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.430
Yes, some people could naturally come across
as more confident than others and it could

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.500
be from positive reinforcement, from their
families telling them how amazing they are,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.479
or a good mentor or a wife that tells them
how amazing -- yes, all of that plays a very

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:10.500
big role.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.780
There is a role that plays with that.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.640
But some cultures, some nationalities, they're
not raised in an environment where somebody's

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.440
telling them how amazing they are.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:25.069
If you come from the Middle East, the Asian
community, that community is not about "Oh,

00:02:25.069 --> 00:02:27.299
you're so awesome, you're going to do so great
things."

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:30.040
No, it's like, "you didn't do this, you didn't
do that."

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:37.819
So there is a part that plays a role, but
not as big as we think.

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:44.170
But the thing that I brought up is, I said,
"Look, if you don't have confidence in yourself,

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:49.650
it's because what you say and what you do
are not aligned.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.260
So what do I mean by that?

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:56.540
If you say, "Hey, the key to success is hard
work" but you're not working hard, you don't

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.819
have confidence, because you know you're not
being honest with the man in the mirror, or

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:03.280
the woman in the mirror, right?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.760
If you say, "you know, you've got to save
money" but then if you're not saving money,

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.840
because internally you're having a battle
that no one sees, it's a hypocritical battle,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.489
because inside, you don't respect yourself
because you know what you are saying is not

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:26.109
what you're doing, so you don't feel good
about yourself, so there's a lack of confidence

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:27.109
in you.

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:31.901
So, the people who have a lot of confidence,
what they say and what they do, they have

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.489
a lot of belief in it.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:36.120
Because they're doing it.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.281
The key to success in business is if you work
hard, and go out there and you make the calls,

00:03:41.281 --> 00:03:45.719
you do this, you do that, and you're doing
it, people are going to buy.

00:03:45.719 --> 00:03:53.709
And so then the other side of it comes, where
it's having leadership with influence.

00:03:53.709 --> 00:03:54.709
Leadership with influence.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:58.060
So one is confidence -- so you have confidence
in you; it's an internal battle.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.430
It's an internal game.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.459
You vs. You.

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:01.459
Right?

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:02.459
Confidence.

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:04.840
Then you have people that you say, "Man, how
does this person have so much influence over

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.140
people?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:12.409
Why is it that these people respond to what
he has to say or what she has to say?"

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:13.409
Right?

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:15.849
That comes down to what?

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:16.849
Moral authority.

00:04:16.849 --> 00:04:18.950
And here's what moral authority is.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:27.000
If what you are doing and what you are saying
is aligned in your mind, and then eventually,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.990
you now have the moral authority for you to
talk about that, because you know the details

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:39.180
about how to have confidence in business and
succeed, then others listen to you and then

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.440
you have influence.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:46.710
Now all there certain anomalies of people
that write a key to success and the next thing

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:51.140
you know, the book blows up and, you know,
but they've never really worked hard, they

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.730
just wrote a book that did very good.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.740
Yes, there are some people like that.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.330
But I don't want to subscribe to the anomaly.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.510
I don't want to subscribe to the exception.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:02.210
I want to figure out a formula that I can
replicate, that can bring me results.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.430
That's what I'm looking for.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:11.320
So, if you're looking for confidence, always
always ask yourself if what you say is it

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.230
what you do?

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.980
What you do, is it aligned with what you say?

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.700
If it is, you believe in yourself.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.600
If it's not, you don't like yourself.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.870
And when you don't like yourself, you're insecure,
you don't like what you're doing, you don't

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:29.490
really like being around, you yourself, you
don't like this person because this person

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.110
is full of it.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.170
There's not an alignment with what this guy
believes and does.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.100
There's a lot of internal battles.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.210
And let me tell you, the worst type of battles
are not a battle with anybody else outside.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:45.760
The worst, most painful, frustrating battles
I've ever faced in my life is me against me.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.760
Biggest.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:47.780
It's never been against anybody else.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.250
It's been me against me.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.330
It's been Pat vs. Pat.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:57.680
It's been the biggest battles of my life is
Pat vs. Pat -- nothing else.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.880
So once these words match the behavior, confidence
goes up.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:08.050
And once enough people start realizing that
what you say and what you do matches the behavior,

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:13.140
moral authority leads to influence, leads
to action, leads to other people wanting to

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:18.740
work with you, to learn from you, to be around
you, to be influence by you, then there's

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:25.270
success, there's growth, there's results,
then there's lifestyle, then there's credibility,

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:29.530
then there's a man sitting in the car next
to you driving like a race car driver.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.400
Tom, this is like you're thinking you're a
race car driver right now.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:39.500
You should see how he's driving.That's the
food that dropped from Raffi's place.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.300
It sounded more like a body.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:52.400
It's like a rental car we got and we haven't
checked the trunk yet.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:55.590
So another thought is we're here in California,
and let me tell you what California freaks

00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:00.780
out the most -- when I wear this shirt, and
I'm walking around with this shirt, oooohhhh,

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.060
they love this shirt.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.290
I love capitalism.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.450
I love capitalism.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.950
And I get some people that commented and say,
"Who are you?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.300
You're the worst person in the world, promoting
capitalism.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.440
I thought you were a nice person."

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:21.070
So just because I believe in capitalism I'm
a bad person now?

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:25.800
Anyways, so if you haven't subscribed to the
channel, please do so.

